blueline: cellular control bridge (UniXNU/QcomBaseband dd0199cf3300, BSD-2), boot-arg bluecell=1

QcomBaseband publishes AppleBaseband, AppleBasebandPCIControl, the PCIe channel
interfaces (pbl, sahara, qmux1/2...), the PDP manager and AppleIPAppender, and
bridges ABM's QMUX to the modem's QMI over QRTR. iOS 16.7's libIOABP and
libTelephonyBasebandDynamic use the same channel and control selectors as the
reference's iOS 17. The board side is ours: QRTR servers and client-port data
from blueline_wifi.c (0165), sends and polling on the modem watcher. Needs
bluewifi>=4 (modem + GLINK) and bluewifi_watch=0. No data path (IPA v3.5.1):
PDP sends fail. MiniIPAppender (0199) now publishes the bridge's AppleIPAppender
(one class of that name), which refuses every method without bluecell.

